{
  "_": [
    "The Maltese, laid out the way Art/sheets.json lays out the cat so the same",
    "script reads both. These sheets are not raw generations: Seedream would not",
    "keep to a 4x4 grid, so each animation was drawn as a loose row of frames,",
    "every frame cut out, taken down to the 48x32 art grid at one scale per",
    "animation, and laid back into a sheet at 8 pixels per art pixel. The cutting",
    "already did what `still` does for the cat: idle is one tailless body with",
    "each frame's tail added, and the blink cells are those frames with the eyes",
    "closed by hand. `spin` is front, three-quarter, side and back from one",
    "generation, with the far side mirrored rather than drawn.",
    "",
    "Scripts/make-sprites.py maltese turns this into MalteseFrames.swift."
  ],
  "cell": 384,
  "block": 8,
  "animations": [
    {
      "name": "idle",
      "sheet": "idle.png",
      "cells": [
        1,
        8
      ],
      "loop": true,
      "fps": 8,
      "view": "front",
      "note": "sitting, tail wagging",
      "blink": [
        9,
        16
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "sleep",
      "sheet": "sleep.png",
      "cells": [
        1,
        8
      ],
      "loop": true,
      "fps": 6,
      "view": "side",
      "note": "curled up, breathing"
    },
    {
      "name": "bristle",
      "sheet": "bristle.png",
      "cells": [
        1,
        7
      ],
      "loop": false,
      "fps": 8,
      "view": "side",
      "note": "startled: jumps, fur puffed out"
    },
    {
      "name": "stretch",
      "sheet": "stretch.png",
      "cells": [
        1,
        8
      ],
      "loop": false,
      "fps": 8,
      "view": "side",
      "note": "a play bow"
    },
    {
      "name": "shake",
